- [P2] Coerce auto-filled defaults in positional args — /home/g/wt/paramsight/active/review-branch/src/paramsight/_paramsight.py:131-131
  When a later PEP 696 default is auto-filled into `__args__` for a partial specialization, Python stores the raw default there (`class C[T, U = None]`; `C[int].__args__ == (int, None)`, and similarly strings remain raw). This positional branch only substitutes typevars, so `C[int]` resolves `U` to `None`/`"Foo"` while the bare default branch resolves to `NoneType`/`ForwardRef`, and `TypeVarValueOption` can mistake a real `None` default for unresolved. Coerce `args[i]` before substituting here as well.

